WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:02.712
Start with a single human demonstration.

2
00:00:03.466 --> 00:00:06.048
Reconstruct the scene
where contact matters.

3
00:00:06.764 --> 00:00:10.271
Mark the supporting hand and
the object's grasp point.

4
00:00:11.683 --> 00:00:13.553
Retarget the motion to the humanoid,

5
00:00:13.808 --> 00:00:16.528
preserving contact with
the table and object.

6
00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:19.852
Change object positions
to create new motions

7
00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:21.194
that reach different targets,

8
00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:23.669
while keeping the support contact fixed.

9
00:00:26.011 --> 00:00:28.244
These examples train a motion generator,

10
00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:32.006
allowing the robot to adapt
to new contact locations.

11
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.462
Reinforcement learning then
trains a control policy

12
00:00:37.472 --> 00:00:39.580
in simulation to track these motions,

13
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:42.392
maintain balance, and complete the pickup.

14
00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:50.179
Finally, the learned
policy transfers zero-shot

15
00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:51.559
to the real humanoid.

16
00:00:51.814 --> 00:00:53.509
It uses the table for support,

17
00:00:53.802 --> 00:00:56.122
reaches under it, and picks up the object.

